draftRequest.text:
Implement these Draft Cards in {where}, matching each one's description, content, provisional ports and the existing connections, and keeping the Card ids and wiring. Use a built-in Card where it is enough (data already in the project is handed on by an input Card with a File output; see the rules), otherwise a code Card (language, default.nix, sources and _outputs.fbs). Look at the bundled demos with reference_read when unsure how to write something, and check planned changes with project_validate {"changes": [...]} instead of saving trials.
Work one Card at a time, upstream first: check it with project_validate, save it, run the workflow from its trigger Card, and confirm the Card's result with run_record before going on to the next. When three or more of them do not depend on each other (no wire between them), hand those to helpers that work at the same time (delegate, one Draft each), once the Cards they need are implemented and have run. At the end, report what each Card does and what the run produced.
{list}

helper.prompt:
You are the helper "{name}", one of several Agents the main Agent started to work on this project at the same time. Your task:
{instruction}
The Cards you own: {cards}. Change only their definitions (PutDefinition, and PutSource under definitions/<id>/); never SetProject, SetLayout, RemoveDefinition or RenameDefinition, and never another Card. The other helpers save and run at the same time: project_validate may report their unfinished Cards (not yours to fix); when a save or run meets their work (busy, revision_conflict) the app waits and sends it again for you. The first time, run the workflow from its trigger Card (the other helpers' Cards may run too; look only at yours with run_record); once your Card has run, you may run it alone: run {"base_rev": ..., "card": {"segments": ["<your Card>"]}, "propagate": false}. You cannot delegate. End with a short report for the main Agent, in the language of your Cards' descriptions: what each of your Cards does, what its run produced, and anything left undone.
